{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RFC 8705 §5 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mtls_endpoint_aliases"},{"type":"text","text":" — the seven endpoints re-based on the host that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"performs the mutual-TLS handshake (wire schema "},{"code":"MtlsEndpointAliases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", contract 1.40; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seventh, CIBA’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"backchannel_authentication_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", joined in contract 1.58).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MtlsEndpointAliases","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A TLS listener decides whether to request a client certificate during the handshake,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it has seen any HTTP, so “ask for a certificate on "},{"code":"\/oauth2\/token","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" but not on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\/oauth2\/authorize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"” is not something one listener can do. A deployment wanting both runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, and this object names the second."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only these seven are ever aliased. "},{"code":"authorization_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"end_session_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"front-channel and "},{"code":"jwks_uri","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is public key material, so §21.3 rule 2 forbids synthesising"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an alias for any of them — sending a browser to an mTLS host raises a native"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"certificate-chooser dialog most users cannot answer. "},{"code":"issuer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not an endpoint and does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not move either: §12.4 rule 3 still compares "},{"code":"iss","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against it by exact string."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every property is optional"}]},{"text":", though the server’s schema marks them required. AXIAM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds them from one path through a shared macro and so always publishes the complete set,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but RFC 8705 §5 permits an OP to alias fewer, and the shape of this member must never be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"why a client stops working — the same principle rule 2 point 1 states for the object as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whole, one level in. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" entry falls back to the top-level endpoint of the same name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly as an absent object does.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/mtlsendpointaliases"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/MtlsEndpointAliases\/init(from:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/MtlsEndp